{"book":"PSA","chapter":142,"source":"hbo","verses":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8],"records":[{"id":"PSA.142.1.s1","verses":[1],"source":"מַשְׂכִּ֥יל לְדָוִ֑ד בִּהְיוֹת֖וֹ בַמְּעָרָ֣ה תְפִלָּֽה׃","gloss":"A maskil of David, when he was in the cave. A prayer.","pieces":[[1,"A maskil of David, when he was in the cave. A prayer.",null]],"L":{"1":"A maskil of David, when he was in the cave. A prayer."},"R":{"1":"A song to teach, by David, from the time when he was in the cave. A prayer."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"punctuation","tokens":["o191420010011","o191420010021","o191420010022","o191420010031","o191420010032","o191420010033","o191420010041","o191420010042","o191420010051"],"choice":"The title is verse 1","alternatives":[],"reason":"The title is part of the Hebrew text and is counted as verse 1, so the verse numbers here are one higher than in Bibles that print the title without a number.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191420010011"],"choice":"maskil: a song of insight, or a skillful song","alternatives":["a teaching poem","an artful song"],"reason":"As in 32:1. The word comes from the verb \"to have insight, act wisely\"; its exact sense as a heading is no longer known.","uncertain":true,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"allusion","tokens":["o191420010031","o191420010042"],"choice":"David in the cave: 1 Samuel 22 and 24","alternatives":[],"reason":"David hid from Saul in the cave of Adullam (1 Samuel 22:1) and in a cave near En-gedi (1 Samuel 24). The title of Psalm 57 also speaks of the cave.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m4","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191420010051"],"choice":"a prayer","alternatives":[],"reason":"The word (tefillah) also heads Psalms 17, 86, 90 and 102.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o191420010011"],"choice":"a song to teach","alternatives":["maskil"],"reason":"As in 32:1, Readable gives the likeliest sense of the term (m2).","uncertain":true,"footnote":false}],"heading":"A prayer from the cave","status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.142.2.s1","verses":[2],"source":"ק֭וֹלִי אֶל־יְהוָ֣ה אֶזְעָ֑ק ק֝וֹלִ֗י אֶל־יְהוָ֥ה אֶתְחַנָּֽן׃","gloss":"[With] my voice to YHWH I cry out; [with] my voice to YHWH I plead for favor.","pieces":[[2,"I call out loud to {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}; I raise my voice to {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}, pleading for mercy.",null]],"L":{"2":"[With] my voice I cry out to {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}; [with] my voice I plead with {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} for mercy."},"R":{"2":"I cry out to {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} for help. I beg {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} to be kind to me."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191420020081"],"choice":"plead for favor: beg for mercy","alternatives":[],"reason":"The verb (chanan, reflexive) is to ask for grace or favor from one who has power to give it (30:9).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191420020041"],"choice":"cry out: call for help in distress","alternatives":[],"reason":"The verb (za'aq) is the cry of someone in trouble (22:6; 107:13).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.142.3.s1","verses":[3],"source":"אֶשְׁפֹּ֣ךְ לְפָנָ֣יו שִׂיחִ֑י צָ֝רָתִ֗י לְפָנָ֥יו אַגִּֽיד׃","gloss":"I pour out before him my complaint; my trouble before him I declare.","pieces":[[3,"I spill out my complaint in front of {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}}; I tell {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}} all about my distress.",null]],"L":{"3":"I pour out before {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}} my complaint; my trouble before {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}} I declare."},"R":{"3":"I tell {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}} everything that is bothering me. I tell {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}} all my troubles."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191420030031"],"choice":"complaint: an anxious pouring out of thoughts","alternatives":["my musing","my lament"],"reason":"The word (siach) is talk or musing, often troubled thought spoken aloud (55:3; 102:1).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"idiom","tokens":["o191420030011"],"choice":"pour out: speak everything without holding back","alternatives":[],"reason":"As water is poured out, so the heart is poured out before God (62:9).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"grammar","tokens":["o191420030023","o191420030053"],"choice":"him: the LORD","alternatives":[],"reason":"The psalmist speaks of the LORD in the third person here, and turns to address him in verse 4.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.142.4.s1","verses":[4],"source":"בְּהִתְעַטֵּ֬ף עָלַ֨י׀רוּחִ֗י וְאַתָּה֮ יָדַ֪עְתָּ נְֽתִיבָ֫תִ֥י בְּאֹֽרַח־ז֥וּ אֲהַלֵּ֑ךְ טָמְנ֖וּ פַ֣ח לִֽי׃","gloss":"When it faints upon me, my spirit — and you, you know my path; in [the] way [that] I walk they have hidden a trap for me.","pieces":[[4,"When my spirit is fading within me, {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} are the one who knows my path. Along the road I travel they have hidden a trap for me.",null]],"L":{"4":"When my spirit grows faint within me, [then] {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} — {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} know my path. In [the] way [where] I walk they have hidden a trap for me."},"R":{"4":"When I feel too weak to go on, {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} know the way I am going. People have hidden a trap on the road where I walk."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191420040012"],"choice":"faints: grows weak, is spent","alternatives":[],"reason":"The same verb (hit'attef) is used in 77:4 and 143:4: the strength to go on is failing.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191420040051"],"choice":"you know my path: you see it and watch over it","alternatives":[],"reason":"God's knowing is caring attention (1:6; 31:8). He sees the path, and the traps on it.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"grammar","tokens":["o191420040042"],"choice":"you: stressed","alternatives":[],"reason":"The pronoun is written out: \"you\", and no one else, knows.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o191420040101"],"choice":"people","alternatives":["they"],"reason":"Readable says who \"they\" are in plain words: the psalmist's enemies.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.142.5.s1","verses":[5],"source":"הַבֵּ֤יט יָמִ֨ין׀וּרְאֵה֮ וְאֵֽין־לִ֪י מַ֫כִּ֥יר אָבַ֣ד מָנ֣וֹס מִמֶּ֑נִּי אֵ֖ין דּוֹרֵ֣שׁ לְנַפְשִֽׁי׃","gloss":"Look [to the] right and see: and there is not for me one who takes notice; refuge has perished from me; there is not one who seeks for my soul.","pieces":[[5,"Look to my right and see: there is no one who knows me. Every way of escape is gone; nobody looks out for me.",null]],"L":{"5":"Look [to the] right and see: there is no one who takes notice of me; refuge has perished from me; there is no one who cares for my soul."},"R":{"5":"Look beside me and see. No one there knows me or pays attention to me. I have no place to run to. No one cares what happens to me."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"culture","tokens":["o191420050021"],"choice":"the right: where a defender stands","alternatives":[],"reason":"In a court or a battle the helper stood at a person's right hand (16:8; 109:31). No one stands there for the psalmist.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"text_variant","tokens":["o191420050011","o191420050032"],"choice":"look and see: commands to God","alternatives":["I look to the right and see (the ancient Greek and other translations)"],"reason":"The Hebrew has forms that are best read as commands, \"look\" and \"see\". Ancient translations read \"I look ... and see\". The sense is much the same.","uncertain":true,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191420050061"],"choice":"one who takes notice: one who recognizes me as a friend","alternatives":[],"reason":"The verb (nakar) is to recognize; here, to own someone as a friend (Ruth 2:10).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m4","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"idiom","tokens":["o191420050071","o191420050081"],"choice":"refuge has perished from me: there is no escape","alternatives":[],"reason":"The word (manos) is a place to flee to (59:17). For him it is lost.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.142.6.s1","verses":[6],"source":"זָעַ֥קְתִּי אֵלֶ֗יךָ יְה֫וָ֥ה אָ֭מַרְתִּי אַתָּ֣ה מַחְסִ֑י חֶ֝לְקִ֗י בְּאֶ֣רֶץ הַֽחַיִּים׃","gloss":"I cry out to you, YHWH; I say, You [are] my refuge, my portion in [the] land of the living.","pieces":[[6,"I cry out to {{deity_pronoun:you|You}}, {{divine_name:LORD|Yahweh}}. I say, \"You are my shelter, all I have in the land of the living.\"",null]],"L":{"6":"I have cried out to {{deity_pronoun:you|You}}, {{divine_name:LORD|Yahweh}}; I have said, \"You [are] my refuge, my portion in the land of the living.\""},"R":{"6":"{{divine_name:LORD|Yahweh}}, I cry out to {{deity_pronoun:you|You}}. I say, \"You are the place where I am safe. You are all I have while I am alive.\""},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191420060071"],"choice":"my portion: my share, all that is mine","alternatives":[],"reason":"A portion (cheleq) was a family's share of the land. The Levites had no land; the LORD was their portion (Numbers 18:20). The psalmist says the same (16:5; 73:26).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"idiom","tokens":["o191420060082","o191420060092"],"choice":"the land of the living: this life","alternatives":[],"reason":"As in 27:13 and 116:9, the world of the living, in contrast to the place of the dead.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191420060061"],"choice":"refuge: a shelter to run to","alternatives":[],"reason":"As in 46:2 (machaseh).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o191420060071"],"choice":"all I have","alternatives":["my portion"],"reason":"Balanced and Readable say what the portion means (m1).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.142.7.s1","verses":[7],"source":"הַקְשִׁ֤יבָה׀אֶֽל־רִנָּתִי֮ כִּֽי־דַלּ֪וֹתִ֫י מְאֹ֥ד הַצִּילֵ֥נִי מֵרֹדְפַ֑י כִּ֖י אָמְצ֣וּ מִמֶּֽנִּי׃","gloss":"Pay attention to my cry, for I have been brought low exceedingly; deliver me from those pursuing me, for they are stronger than I.","pieces":[[7,"Pay heed to my cry, because I am in the depths. Rescue me from those who hunt me, since they are stronger than I am.",null]],"L":{"7":"Pay attention to my cry, for I have been brought very low; deliver me from those who pursue me, for they are too strong for me."},"R":{"7":"Please listen to me when I cry for help. I am in deep trouble. Save me from the people who are chasing me. They are stronger than I am."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"allusion","tokens":["o191420070101","o191420070111"],"choice":"stronger than I: as in Psalm 18:18","alternatives":[],"reason":"The same words are used in 18:18 of David's enemies, from whom God rescued him.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191420070051"],"choice":"brought low: weak, helpless","alternatives":[],"reason":"The verb (dalal) is to be low, poor and weak (79:8; 116:6).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191420070082"],"choice":"those pursuing me: those who hunt me down","alternatives":[],"reason":"As Saul pursued David (1 Samuel 23:25; title, verse 1).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.142.8.s1","verses":[8],"source":"ה֘וֹצִ֤יאָה מִמַּסְגֵּ֨ר׀נַפְשִׁי֮ לְהוֹד֪וֹת אֶת־שְׁ֫מֶ֥ךָ בִּ֭י יַכְתִּ֣רוּ צַדִּיקִ֑ים כִּ֖י תִגְמֹ֣ל עָלָֽי׃","gloss":"Bring out from prison my soul, to give thanks to your name; about me they will surround, [the] righteous, for you will deal fully with me.","pieces":[[8,"Lead me out of this prison, so that I may thank {{deity_pronoun:your|Your}} name. Then the righteous will crowd around me, because {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} will treat me with goodness.",null]],"L":{"8":"Bring my soul out of prison, to give thanks to {{deity_pronoun:your|Your}} name. [The] righteous will gather around me, for {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} will deal bountifully with me."},"R":{"8":"Free me from this prison so I can thank {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} for who {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} are. Then good people will gather around me, because {{deity_pronoun:you|You}} will be good to me."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"idiom","tokens":["o191420080022"],"choice":"prison: the trap of his distress","alternatives":[],"reason":"The prison may be the cave of the title, or a picture of trouble that shuts him in (88:9).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191420080081"],"choice":"will surround me: will gather around me","alternatives":["will crown themselves because of me","will wait for me"],"reason":"The verb (katar) means to surround, or in another form to crown. The righteous will gather to celebrate with him.","uncertain":true,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o191420080111"],"choice":"deal fully: do good, repay with kindness","alternatives":[],"reason":"The verb (gamal) is to deal out in full, here God's goodness (13:6; 116:7).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["B","R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o191420080022"],"choice":"this prison","alternatives":["prison"],"reason":"\"This\" makes clear that the psalmist speaks of the place he is in now.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-2","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o191420080061","o191420080091"],"choice":"for who you are; good people","alternatives":["your name; the righteous"],"reason":"As in 140:14.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"}],"words":{"1":[{"id":"o191420010011","text":"מַשְׂכִּ֥יל","after":" ","lemma":"מַשְׂכִּיל","morph":"Ncmsa","gloss":"a.poem","strong":"4905","transliteration":"maśkiyl","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · common · masculine singular absolute"},{"id":"o191420010021","text":"לְ","after":"","lemma":"לְ","morph":"R","gloss":"of","strong":"3807a","transliteration":"lə","lang":"H","parse":"Preposition"},{"id":"o191420010022","text":"דָוִ֑ד","after":" ","lemma":"דָּוִד","morph":"Np","gloss":"David","strong":"1732","transliteration":"ḏāwiḏ","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · proper name"},{"id":"o191420010031","text":"בִּ","after":"","lemma":"בְּ","morph":"R","gloss":"when","strong":"0871a","transliteration":"bi","lang":"H","parse":"Preposition"},{"id":"o191420010032","text":"הְיוֹת֖","after":"","lemma":"הָיָה","morph":"Vqc","gloss":"was","strong":"1961","transliteration":"","lang":"H","parse":"Verb · Qal · infinitive construct"},{"id":"o191420010033","text":"וֹ","after":" ","lemma":"הוּא","morph":"Sp3ms","gloss":"he","strong":"2050c","transliteration":"","lang":"H","parse":"Suffix · pronoun · 3rd person masculine singular"},{"id":"o191420010041","text":"בַ","after":"","lemma":"בְּ","morph":"Rd","gloss":"in","strong":"0871a","transliteration":"ḇa","lang":"H","parse":"Preposition · with the article"},{"id":"o191420010042","text":"מְּעָרָ֣ה","after":" ","lemma":"מְעָרָה","morph":"Ncfsa","gloss":"cave","strong":"4631","transliteration":"mməʿārāh","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · common · feminine singular absolute"},{"id":"o191420010051","text":"תְפִלָּֽה","after":"׃","lemma":"תְּפִלָּה","morph":"Ncfsa","gloss":"a.prayer","strong":"8605","transliteration":"ṯəp̄illāh:","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · common · feminine singular absolute"}],"2":[{"id":"o191420020011","text":"ק֭וֹלִ","after":"","lemma":"קוֹל","morph":"Ncmsc","gloss":"voice","strong":"6963","transliteration":"","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · common · masculine singular construct (of ...)"},{"id":"o191420020012","text":"י","after":" ","lemma":"הוּא","morph":"Sp1cs","gloss":"my","strong":"2967a","transliteration":"","lang":"H","parse":"Suffix · pronoun · 1st person common singular"},{"id":"o191420020021","text":"אֶל","after":"־","lemma":"אֶל","morph":"R","gloss":"to","strong":"0413","transliteration":"ʾel-","lang":"H","parse":"Preposition"},{"id":"o191420020031","text":"יְהוָ֣ה","after":" ","lemma":"יהוה","morph":"Np","gloss":"Yahweh","strong":"3068","transliteration":"yəhwāh","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · proper name"},{"id":"o191420020041","text":"אֶזְעָ֑ק","after":" ","lemma":"זָעַק","morph":"Vqi1cs","gloss":"I.cry.out","strong":"2199","transliteration":"ʾezʿāq","lang":"H","parse":"Verb · Qal · imperfect (yiqtol) · 1st person common singular"},{"id":"o191420020051","text":"ק֝וֹלִ֗","after":"","lemma":"קוֹל","morph":"Ncmsc","gloss":"voice","strong":"6963","transliteration":"","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · common · masculine singular construct